The watcher's executable jar (bfm-watcher.jar) bundles third-party libraries, each under its own open-source
licence (mostly the Apache License 2.0; also EPL-2.0, EDL-1.0, CDDL-1.0 and MIT), among them Spring Framework,
Spring Boot, Spring Security, Vaadin Flow and its core components, Apache Ratis, Apache Tomcat, Jackson, Logback,
Angus Mail and jsoup. Each library's licence text and notice are inside its own jar (BOOT-INF/lib/*.jar,
under META-INF/).

The console bundles the fonts Plus Jakarta Sans and JetBrains Mono under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
(bfm-watcher/src/main/resources/META-INF/resources/fonts/OFL-*.txt).

The agent (minipgagent.jar) uses the JDK only.
